            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary syndrome associated with coronary aneurysm: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An elderly female patient presented to our Emergency Department with an acute coronary syndrome. After stabilization, cardiac catheterization disclosed a solitary aneurysm of her diagonal coronary artery. Such aneurysms are rare and are an unusual etiology for acute coronary syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
